# Search defaults for ripgrep and fd (round 108).  This file is NOT a
# .gitignore: nothing listed here is untracked, and git does not read it.
# It exists because ~57% of every repo-wide search hit was v3 — measured
# 2026-08-24: `style` 457 hits repo-wide against 189 outside v3,
# `renderer` 213/117, `boundingBox` 116/73, `controlPoints` 37/20 — a
# codebase agents and people are usually not working on, drowning the one
# they are.
#
# v3 is still searched deliberately, for parity questions.  Do it
# explicitly, and the flag is the whole difference:
#
#     rg --no-ignore -g 'v3/**' <pattern>
#     rg --no-ignore -e 'cy.on' v3/documentation/docmaker.json
#
v3/

# Build output: regenerated, never read for meaning.  (`build/`, `dist/`
# and `node_modules/` are already hidden by .gitignore, which rg reads.)
status/
test-results/
playwright-report/
